    "question": {
      ":question/id": "461967d1-8106-5690-8e41-619893730384",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}$ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\left(y-1\\right)<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 \\cos^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} \\\\ (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\sec^{2}{\\left(y - 1 \\right)})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)} & =2 x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\tan{\\left(y - 1 \\right)}=2 x+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
